--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Components under their own terms
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The above covers piegpu's own code. These parts came from elsewhere and keep
the licences they arrived with (the README's "Third-party software" lists
them all, with what each is used for):

  gpu/audio/faad2/          FAAD2 (libfaad), GPL-2.0-or-later, with its
                            COPYING file.

  gpu/audio/minimp3/        minimp3, CC0 1.0, with its LICENSE file.

  gpu/video/userland/       The MMAL client of the Raspberry Pi userland,
                            BSD-3-Clause, with its LICENCE file.

  demos/jet/Jet/            Jet, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 CubeCoders Limited,
                            with its LICENSE file.

  demos/jet/examples/       Scenes from CubeCoders' JetExamples, MIT, with
                            their LICENSE file.

  demos/jet/viewer/,        From picojet, BSD-2-Clause, Copyright (c) 2026,
  demos/jet/runtime/        Andrei Nigmatulin (the parts demos/jet/README.md
  (parts)                   names as picojet's).

  demos/assets/             Meshes and textures converted by picojet's tools:
                              radio, column, biplane: opengameart.org, CC0;
                              cube, f117, f22, efa, sphere, crab, the pikuma
                              texture: shipped with the renderer from Gustavo
                              Pezzi's pikuma.com 3D graphics course, and
                              retained under whatever terms they arrived with.

  third_party/              Submodules, each under its own licence: Circle
                            (GPL-3.0), Mesa (MIT and others), VK-GL-CTS
                            (Apache-2.0), the Raspberry Pi userland
                            (BSD-3-Clause).

The RPi firmware built from gpu/ links Circle (GPL-3.0) and FAAD2
(GPL-2.0-or-later): the firmware binaries (kernel.img, kernel8.img) are
therefore distributed under the GPL, version 3; their source is this
repository and its submodules. They run with the Raspberry Pi's own firmware
(bootcode.bin, start.elf, fixup.dat), which is distributed in binary form
under Broadcom's licence (third_party/circle/boot/LICENCE.broadcom).
